<%# The whole list is one Turbo Stream target. Adding or removing a row moves
    money in every other row, so redrawing the list as a unit is one action that
    cannot leave the rows and the amounts disagreeing — where appending the new
    row and then patching each other row would be a dozen actions that can. %>
<ol id="participants">
  <%= render partial: "participants/participant_row",
             collection: split.participants,
             as: :participant,
             locals: {
               split: split,
               removable: split.participants.size > SplitMath::PEOPLE_RANGE.min
             } %>
</ol>
